From: baf <oibaf.vallo@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rtw88: force 6 Mbps for RTL8821CS 5 GHz EAPOL

RTL8821CS over SDIO can intermittently delay or fail EAPOL
transmissions on 5 GHz when they are left to firmware rate adaptation,
causing WPA 4-way handshake timeouts.

For RTL8821C SDIO on 5 GHz only, force EAPOL frames to the robust
6 Mbps OFDM rate and disable rate fallback. Leave all normal data
traffic under the existing firmware rate-control path.

Signed-off-by: baf <oibaf.vallo@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/tx.c b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/tx.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/tx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/tx.c
@@ -647,6 +647,21 @@
 	pkt_info->stbc = stbc;
 	pkt_info->ldpc = ldpc;
 
+	/*
+	 * RTL8821CS SDIO can intermittently fail to transmit EAPOL frames
+	 * reliably on 5 GHz when using firmware rate adaptation.  Use the
+	 * robust 6 Mbps OFDM rate for EAPOL while leaving normal data traffic
+	 * under firmware rate control.
+	 */
+	if (rtwdev->chip->id == RTW_CHIP_TYPE_8821C &&
+	    rtwdev->hci.type == RTW_HCI_TYPE_SDIO &&
+	    rtwdev->hal.current_band_type == RTW_BAND_5G &&
+	    skb->protocol == cpu_to_be16(ETH_P_PAE)) {
+		pkt_info->rate = DESC_RATE6M;
+		pkt_info->dis_rate_fallback = true;
+		pkt_info->use_rate = true;
+	}
+
 	fix_rate = dm_info->fix_rate;
 	if (fix_rate < DESC_RATE_MAX) {
 		pkt_info->rate = fix_rate;
